/target
**/target
# Wasm build output (regenerate with scripts/build-wasm.sh)
/res
node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store

# Next.js build output
.next/
# artefacts that rode along with the copied Float dashboard
apps/dashboard/.localappdata/
apps/dashboard/build-output.txt
apps/dashboard/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
apps/dashboard/git

# testnet demo agent keys - never commit
.demo/

# Secret-bearing. `.float/` holds agent private keys and the quote-signer
# secret written by create-float. It also carries its own `.gitignore`, but
# that file is only created when the wizard runs and can be deleted — this
# entry is the one that does not depend on anything else being present.
.float/
.tmpcreds/
packages/create-float/SKILL.md

# MCP server config. UNTRACKED ON PURPOSE, for two independent reasons:
#
#   1. It holds an ABSOLUTE machine-specific path (`C:\Users\<name>\...`),
#      because relative paths in `args` are not supported — they go straight to
#      the OS process launcher rather than being resolved against the project
#      root. So it was never shareable between machines regardless.
#
#   2. Enabling `vault_pay` means putting NEAR_VAULT_AGENT_KEY in it, and that
#      is a private key. This repo already carries a scar from a CLI that
#      echoed one into a terminal and a chat transcript — which is why every
#      script here signs with `sign-with-access-key-file` rather than a
#      plaintext key. A TRACKED file that users are told to paste a key into is
#      a leak waiting to happen.
#
# Regenerate with: node scripts/print-mcp-command.mjs
.mcp.json

# Scratch build dir for a second dev server (see next.config.ts)
.next-preview/

# Local agent state, not project source.
# .claude/worktrees holds a FULL COPY of this repository - 1.2 GB measured -
# so committing this directory would add the repo to itself.
.claude/

# the gate's own dashboard build output (scripts/verify-all.mjs)
apps/dashboard/.next-verify/

# MCP client config and its backups: these carry NEAR_VAULT_AGENT_KEY inline on
# some setups, so they are LIVE PRIVATE KEYS. `.mcp.json.bak` was committed and
# pushed on 2026-11-12 by a `git add -A` after a script wrote the backup --
# the key was for a testnet vault that does not exist, so it controlled
# nothing, but the mechanism would have leaked a mainnet key just as readily.
# Ignored by PATTERN, not by name, so the next backup is covered too.
.mcp.json
.mcp.json.bak
*.bak

# Copied from the root SKILL.md by packages/mcp prepack — one source of bytes.
packages/mcp/SKILL.md

# Demo script: kept locally for filming, not published.
DEMO.md
